  "limitations": [
    "Variant F treats any non-empty hint as an accessible name. Hints can be placeholders ('Enter text'), so this is an upper bound on what a screen reader would usefully announce, as the primary measure is a lower bound.",
    "The fallback flag is reconstructed from node depths, not read from the parse, because the parser's used_ancestor_fallback column records a non-clickable result instead. The reconstruction applies the parser's own rule to the stored nodes; the script stops if any resolved click contradicts it.",
    "The fallback-free RQ3 rows drop fallback touches from the touched set only. The background keeps elements of the same kind, mostly clickable wrappers of role 'other', so those rows bound the direction of any fallback bias rather than estimate a bias-free difference.",
    "AndroidControl app identity comes from resource-id packages. An app whose views carry no resource ids, or one that spans several packages, can be split across clusters, which would narrow the app-level interval slightly."
  ]
}